# Logseq tasks - markers, priorities, scheduling
# https://docs.logseq.com/#/page/tasks

## Workflow markers (first word of the block)
LATER -> NOW  -> DONE            default flavour
TODO  -> DOING -> DONE           alternate flavour (Settings > preferred workflow)
CANCELED / CANCELLED             typed directly, not in the cycle
IN-PROGRESS
WAIT / WAITING
# mod+enter cycles the marker while editing; /LATER etc. also work.
# Clicking the empty checkbox jumps straight to DONE.

## Priorities
LATER [#A] ship the thing        highest   (/A)
LATER [#B] the middling thing    mid       (/B)
LATER [#C] the someday thing     lowest    (/C)
# `[#X]` goes after the marker, before the text.

## Scheduled and deadline (own lines, below the block text)
DEADLINE: <2021-05-29 Sat>       /Deadline
SCHEDULED: <2021-05-31 Mon>      /Scheduled
SCHEDULED: <2021-05-26 Wed 7:00> with a time
# Both work on non-task blocks too.
# :scheduled/future-days in config.edn controls the look-ahead window.

## Repeaters (append to the timestamp; "Add repeater" in the date picker)
SCHEDULED: <2021-05-26 Wed 7:00 .+1d>    repeat 1d after you mark it DONE
SCHEDULED: <2021-05-26 Wed ++1w>         next same weekday, from today
SCHEDULED: <2021-05-26 Wed +1m>          fixed 1m from the original date

## Time tracking
# Marking NOW/DOING writes a :LOGBOOK: drawer under the block.
# Disable it in Settings > enable timetracking.

## Finding tasks
{{query (task now later)}}                    simple query
{{query (and (task now) (priority a))}}
{{query (and (task todo) (between -7d today))}}
# Advanced/datalog equivalents: see logseq/datalog and logseq/schema.

## Journal defaults
# The "NOW" / "NEXT" query blocks at the bottom of today's journal come from
